        "summary":  "Abnormal AI deployed Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Code Interpreter to power real-time email threat detection agents processing billions of messages daily. The company uses a three-tiered architecture where lightweight classifiers handle high-volume screening, ML models address uncertain cases, and AI agents with sandbox execution analyze complex threats inline. An additional batch-mode analyst agent autonomously identifies patterns and generates improved heuristics feeding back into the detection pipeline.",
        "execSummary":  "Abnormal AI demonstrates production-scale agentic security processing billions of emails through a tiered detection system that reserves expensive agent compute for the highest-confidence decisions, offering a replicable architecture pattern for any high-volume enterprise workflow. By leveraging Code Interpreter\u0027s managed sandbox environment, the company achieves zero-trust security posture while enabling agents to perform computational analysis beyond simple language reasoning. Key operational lessons include treating Code Interpreter as fundamental agent infrastructure for compute-heavy reasoning tasks, implementing programmatic verification guardrails, and designing long-running batch jobs with checkpoints to transcend session time limits. This case study is directly transferable to enterprise customer-support organizations looking to build scalable, cost-controlled agentic triage systems.",
