        "theme":  "Orchestration",
        "summary":  "The article describes a dual-layer monitoring architecture for production AI agent systems, combining Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Evaluations for continuous quality assessment with AWS DevOps Agent for autonomous infrastructure investigation. The authors demonstrate this approach through an airline reservation system using four specialized agents coordinated via the Swarm pattern. The architecture shows how quality metrics and infrastructure monitoring must work together to catch both agent effectiveness failures and silent infrastructure issues.",
        "execSummary":  "For enterprise leaders deploying multi-agent systems, traditional infrastructure monitoring proves insufficient because agents can fail silently without surfacing errors and tool selections can be incorrect despite successful execution. This solution implements two complementary layers: AgentCore Evaluations continuously scores live interactions on helpfulness, correctness, and goal completion, while AWS DevOps Agent autonomously investigates infrastructure incidents by correlating logs, metrics, and service interactions across system boundaries. The dual approach transforms production data into actionable improvement cycles, enabling faster incident resolution and continuous agent optimization without requiring manual investigation. This is a critical operations model for any enterprise moving agentic AI from pilot to production support systems.",
