        "execSummary":  "This framework addresses a critical enterprise decision: determining the appropriate level of AI model customization without over-engineering or under-investing in foundation model adaptation. The methodology recommends starting with the simplest intervention — improved prompting — and escalating only when specific performance gaps emerge, noting that most workloads never need to advance past RAG, significantly reducing unnecessary infrastructure investment. For customer-support and enterprise AI leaders, this provides a structured decision tree that aligns technical investment with measurable business outcomes rather than following technology trend cycles. The framework also helps justify build-vs-buy decisions internally by anchoring customization choices to concrete capability gaps rather than vendor recommendations.",
