        "execSummary":  "The enterprise AI infrastructure landscape is shifting from compute-limited to power-limited scaling, and NVIDIA DSX represents a comprehensive platform response addressing the most acute challenge: delivering maximum computational output within fixed power budgets through integrated hardware and software co-design. Early deployments prove substantial real-world gains — approximately 25% efficiency improvement at Lambda — while production grid-integration capabilities now enable data centers to participate in demand response without compromising critical workloads. For enterprise leaders evaluating AI infrastructure investments, this reframes the ROI calculation: efficiency gains directly unlock stranded capacity, meaning existing facilities can serve significantly more workloads without new power procurement. Organizations planning AI factory expansions should factor tokens-per-watt into infrastructure RFPs alongside traditional cost-per-GPU metrics.",
