        "execSummary":  "NVIDIA is repositioning AI infrastructure optimization around energy efficiency metrics rather than peak performance alone, with Vera Rubin NVL72 systems combined with DSX MaxLPS dynamic power allocation enabling operators to deploy up to 40% additional GPU capacity within fixed power budgets. This shift addresses the fundamental constraint of modern data center operations where available power — not computational demand — is the limiting factor for AI factory scaling. For enterprise leaders, this translates to a concrete competitive advantage: organizations that adopt efficiency-first infrastructure strategies can serve significantly more AI workloads within existing facility footprints, deferring costly power and cooling upgrades. The tokens-per-watt metric introduced here is likely to become a standard procurement criterion for enterprise AI infrastructure over the next 12-18 months.",
