        "execSummary":  "Enterprise technology leaders are finding that AI governance cannot be retrofitted onto existing IT risk models — it requires purpose-built frameworks that evolve alongside model capabilities. CIOs who move too slowly on AI risk competitive irrelevance, while those who move without governance frameworks expose their organizations to regulatory and reputational harm. The article argues for a dynamic oversight model that adjusts controls based on use-case risk level rather than applying uniform restrictions. For customer-support leaders, this translates directly into tiered agent autonomy: full automation for low-stakes interactions, mandatory human-in-the-loop for sensitive escalations.",
