        "summary":  "MIT research cited in the article shows 95% of generative AI pilots fail to deliver measurable business impact, with organizational issues rather than technical shortcomings cited as the primary cause. The article provides a framework for identifying warning signs of struggling initiatives, salvaging projects through better governance and workflow integration, and determining when to discontinue efforts entirely.",
        "execSummary":  "With nearly all enterprise gen AI pilots stalling before production, the challenge is no longer adoption speed — it is execution discipline. The article argues that most failures trace back to unclear ownership, insufficient workflow redesign, and the absence of success metrics defined before deployment begins. Leaders can recover struggling initiatives by resetting scope to a single high-value use case, assigning a dedicated product owner, and establishing a 90-day proof-of-value checkpoint. For customer-support organizations, this framework applies directly to AI-assisted agent tools that never crossed from pilot to scale.",
