        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/salesforce-launches-aiforce-interface-layer-agentic-architecture/830479/",
        "date":  "2026-09-15",
        "theme":  "Platforms",
        "summary":  "Salesforce unveiled AIforce at Dreamforce 2026, an interface layer that connects the CRM platform\u0027s data, workflows, and governance to third-party AI tools including Claude, ChatGPT, Slack, and Microsoft Teams. CEO Marc Benioff described it as a four-layer enterprise architecture — data, apps and semantics, agents, and interface — that brings Salesforce capabilities to employees wherever they work.",
        "execSummary":  "AIforce positions Salesforce as the connective tissue of enterprise AI rather than just a CRM vendor, enabling organizations to surface CRM data and workflows through any AI interface employees already use. For enterprise leaders, the practical implication is that Salesforce customer data can now be accessed by AI agents and chatbots without custom integration work. Customer-support leaders should evaluate how AIforce interacts with existing contact-center platforms, as it could accelerate deployment of AI-powered service agents with access to full customer history. The multi-interface approach also reduces the risk of shadow AI, since employees can access AI capabilities within governed Salesforce data perimeters.",
