        "execSummary":  "The tooling gap for multi-agent orchestration is becoming a critical bottleneck: even as AI agents become capable of complex tasks, the infrastructure for directing and monitoring them at scale remains immature. Enterprises rushing to deploy agent-based development or operations workflows will encounter this gap directly — agents produce output, but human supervisors lose context and traceability across concurrent streams. This is not just a developer problem; it mirrors the orchestration challenges emerging in AI-powered customer service, where multiple agents may handle different stages of a single interaction. Investment in orchestration tooling and workflow observability should be treated as a prerequisite for any multi-agent enterprise deployment.",
