        "execSummary":  "OpenAI\u0027s managed Agents API lowers the technical barrier to enterprise agent deployment significantly, but the tradeoff is deeper dependency on a single vendor\u0027s infrastructure and data handling practices. For enterprises in regulated sectors — financial services, healthcare, government — the data residency and privacy constraints of a managed cloud API may disqualify it as the primary agent runtime. Technology leaders evaluating this offering should map it against their data governance requirements before committing architecture decisions. The competitive pressure this creates on Microsoft Azure AI, AWS Bedrock, and Google Vertex is likely to accelerate equivalent managed offerings from all major cloud providers within the next 6-12 months.",
