        "summary":  "Boston University research found that framing AI agents as \u0027coworkers\u0027 causes humans to catch 18% fewer errors and increases deference, with workers 44% more likely to escalate AI output to managers rather than verify it themselves. The article argues that marketing AI as digital employees is primarily a sales strategy that actually undermines workplace effectiveness. Researchers and economists advocate instead for optimizing AI to augment human capabilities rather than simulate colleague relationships.",
