        "date":  "2026-07-27",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Intel-sponsored analysis outlines five infrastructure lessons from workload testing for enterprise agentic AI deployment, emphasizing that agentic AI is a full systems challenge covering compute, memory, and networking — not just an inference problem. The piece recommends measuring six operational metrics including task success rate, cost per task, and agent density per vCPU rather than traditional average CPU utilization. Scale-out architectures are recommended over scale-up for agent systems handling distributed, latency-sensitive workloads.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprises moving from AI chatbots to autonomous agents face a fundamentally different infrastructure challenge: existing performance metrics and capacity planning models do not apply. Measuring task latency at P95 and agent density per vCPU — rather than average utilization — gives a more accurate picture of real-world readiness. Scale-out architectures consistently outperform scale-up designs for agent workloads. Leaders should treat agentic AI infrastructure procurement as a strategic business decision with ROI and efficiency criteria, not a purely technical one.",
