        "summary":  "OpenAI developed GPT-Red, an automated red-teaming system that stress-tests its own language models through competitive self-play, simulating real deployment scenarios including web browsing, email access, and code execution. The system discovered a novel \u0027fake chain of thought\u0027 attack vector where malicious instructions are embedded in a model\u0027s reasoning process, an approach that succeeded against 90% of GPT-5 but only 23% of GPT-5.6. While GPT-Red significantly improves automated vulnerability discovery, human red-teaming remains necessary for conversational and image-based attack vectors.",
